INT. MAPLE STREET VET CLINIC - RECEPTION - DAY

Waiting room. Linoleum. A fish tank. A beagle howls from behind a door.

JUNE (17, scrubs two sizes too big, first week) stacks leaflets at the desk. She keeps checking the clock.

LENA OKAFOR (40s, vet, white coat) strides through with a clipboard.

LENA
June. Room two. Now.

JUNE
Yes, Dr. Okafor.

THE CHEN KIDS (three siblings, matching backpacks) sit in a row on the bench, a cat carrier on their laps. It yowls. They flinch together.

RIVER (20s, they/them, nose ring, rescue-shelter hoodie) leans on the counter.

RIVER
Hey. I'm here for my appointment. Biscuit has the thing.

JUNE
What thing?

RIVER
(shrugging)
The thing. Biscuit's a dog. Biscuit has the thing.

A black lab sits at their feet, head cocked.

JUNE
(writing)
Okay. Uh. Name?

RIVER
Biscuit. Last name Rivera-Hall. They go by Biscuit.

JUNE
Who goes by Biscuit?

RIVER
The dog. Me too, honestly.

June blinks. Writes. Her pen skids across the page.

LENA (O.S.)
June! Room two!

JUNE
(under her breath)
Coming, coming, oh my God.

The cat carrier SCREECHES. The Chen Kids scream in unison.

THE CHEN KIDS
It's biting!

RIVER
(calmly)
It's not biting. It's just upset.

JUNE
(to herself, flipping a chart)
Don't panic. Don't panic.

She turns. Grabs the carrier. The cat bolts out the front, a streak of grey fur, knocking over the fish tank stand.

JUNE (CONT'D)
(to the room)
Everybody stay calm!

Nobody is calm.

The front door swings open. MR. HALVERSEN (60s, tweed coat, a parrot on his shoulder) steps in, drenched.

MR. HALVERSEN
Which one of you is in charge?

LENA
(emerging, hands up)
That would be me.

MR. HALVERSEN
My bird says your sign is wrong.

PARROT
(from his shoulder)
Wrong! Wrong!

June puts her head on the desk.

Biscuit the dog barks once, the cat yowls from the street, and the fish tank gently drips onto the floor.
